v1 westbank-alerts — let `complete_json` speak to an OpenAI-compatible endpoint,
so it can be pointed at the brain's gateway instead of the dead subscription.

APPLY AFTER v1-minimax-metrics.patch. From the service root:

    cd /opt/stacks/palestine/services/westbank-alerts
    patch -p1 --dry-run < ~/palestine-v2/ops/patches/v1-minimax-to-gateway.patch
    patch -p1 < ~/palestine-v2/ops/patches/v1-minimax-to-gateway.patch

Then, in that directory's .env (600, root's to edit — the key is NEVER copied
into either repo; read it off the brain at the moment you paste it):

    ssh zaid@100.110.89.116 'cut -d= -f2 /opt/stacks/gateway/.env'   # the key

    MINIMAX_API_STYLE=openai
    MINIMAX_BASE_URL=http://100.110.89.116:4000/v1
    MINIMAX_MODEL=engine
    MINIMAX_API_KEY=<the key that command printed>

    docker compose up -d --build

CHECK IT, DO NOT ASSUME IT:

    curl -s localhost:8081/quality/checkpoints | jq .llm
    # success_rate should stop being 0.0 within the hour
    ~/palestine-v2/.venv/bin/python -m ops.minimax_alarm --dry-run

ROLLBACK is the three .env lines back to MiniMax's, or MINIMAX_ENABLED=false —
the pipeline has always run rules-first and falls back to them on any failure,
which is precisely why three months of total failure changed no output.

WHAT IS NOT DECIDED HERE
Whether to cancel the MiniMax subscription. That is Zaid's call and this patch
does not make it — it only makes the alternative one .env edit away.

